# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  TAG 1 · DECK-GESPRÄCHE und NACHGESPRÄCHE
#
#  REGELN (damit Rowan nie etwas weiß, was er nicht wissen kann)
#    · Ein Deck kommentiert Rowan erst, wenn deck_known_<id> gesetzt ist (Antwort der Person, Duell oder Hinweis im Text).
#    · Raten darf er nur mit Anhaltspunkt (sichtbare Dinge aus der Erstszene) und nicht bei jedem:
#        richtiger Tipp   marit, inya, jessica, victoria, teobalt (allgemein), georgie (Drachen, nur mit Ember), gideon (nur wenn er ihn spielen sah)
#        falscher Tipp    ed (Pferde statt Affen), ashton (Dornen statt Verschmutzung)
#        halbrichtig      sunny (Wasser statt Eis), tomi (Hortet statt zu stehlen)
#        nur Nachfragen   baylee, pippa, mikoto, magnus, noor, livvie, rana (kein Anhaltspunkt)
#        Nathan           sagt sein Deck schon im Prolog; hier nur das Fachsimpeln (shop_nathan).
#    · Nach der Auskunft murmelt Rowan die Karten im Stakkato vor sich hin: er hat das Deck schon hundertmal online gesehen.
#  deck_<id>   wird in den Gesprächen angeboten und vor jedem Duell (setzt deck_known_<id>)
#  post_<id>   Nachgespräch nach dem Duell, getrennt nach Sieg und Niederlage (won:<duell-id>)
#  Karten und Helden stammen aus bible/decks/<id>.json
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ───────────────────────────── DECK-GESPRÄCHE ─────────────────────────────

@scene shop_nathan
  # Nathans Deck ist seit der Begrüßung bekannt; das hier ist reines Fachsimpeln.
  [rowan] "War Counselors. You said best deck in the format. Talk me through it."
  [nathan=happy] "SIX different dudes! Censpartan, Cykyran, Gorinthian, Harpthenean, Minocrete, Thebinxan, I can say them ALL, I practised in the shower! You play one a turn and every dude is better for every OTHER dude on the table. It's basically Thanksgiving!"
  Rowan's eyes have drifted out of focus. His lips are moving a half-second ahead of his voice.
  [rowan] "…One of each at a time. Each one stronger per Counselor out. War Chest pays for the Gathering Place, so the new one acts the turn it lands. Three or four out and the board does everything. Stuns. Doubled shots. Gold cannon." A breath. "Over-commits every game. One sweep and the whole table goes at once. Right. *Right.*"
  [nathan] "…Did you just say *sweep*?"
  [baylee] "He's right."
  [nathan=laughing] "He's — okay, he's right! But nobody sweeps! It's rude!"
  [rowan] "Somebody always sweeps. I'd keep a Counselor in hand until I knew they couldn't."
  [nathan=happy] "A Counselor in HAND. Baylee! He said keep one in HAND! Nobody's ever told me that, they just tell me I'm loud!"
  @aff nathan +2 | Took his deck seriously
  @flag shop_nathan_done
  @time 3

@scene deck_baylee
  @if deck_known_baylee
    @end
  @choice
    > "What do you run, Baylee? Only if you feel like saying."
      [baylee] "Big Stomp. Dinosaurs." He looks at his own hand for a moment. "Not good. Fun, though."
      @aff baylee +1 | Asked about his deck
      @scene mutter_baylee
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_baylee
      @end

@scene mutter_baylee
  @if deck_known_baylee
    @end
  Rowan's eyes have gone to the horizon. He talks to it, low and quick.
  [rowan] "…Güldefaber, Kit, Alex. Training. Performance. Stack the Summoning Magic until one hero can call a Gigantisaur. Four Chimeras to close. Stomp each turn for every hero beside a giant. Pier keeps the hand full." A beat. "Slow. Honest. Heroes sit there for turns."
  [baylee] "…Yup." A very long pause. "You've seen it."
  [rowan] "Online. A few times. Never next to the man who plays it."
  [baylee] "Folks think I'm asleep, those first turns. I'm not asleep."
  @aff baylee +1 | Knew the deck
  @deckinfo baylee

@scene deck_ed
  @if deck_known_ed
    @end
  @choice
    > "Cowboy hat, ranch, boots over the rail. Horses, I'd say. Warhorse, Sun Sword, everything piled on one hero?" @hint From his look
      [ed] "Ha! Nope! Horses are lovely, I'd never say a word against a horse, but no."
      [ed] "**MONKEES!** Two e's! Monkee Rodeo! The hat's for the *Rodeo!* Not the horse!"
      [rowan] "…Monkees. Right. That's — that's a better one than mine."
      @aff ed +1 | Guessed wrong, cheerfully
    > "What do you play, Ed?"
      [ed] "Monkee Rodeo! Two e's! Every time I gain gold a Monkee wakes up and does something! Cheeky ones hit people, Nimble ones come out free, Non-Fungible ones pay twice!"
      [ed] "I don't actually understand the Non-Fungible ones. Dad says it's financial."
      @aff ed +1 | Asked about his deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_ed
      @end
  Rowan has stopped listening to the joke. His eyes are on the sea and his voice drops to a rapid undertone.
  [rowan] "…Gold in, Monkee out. Cheeky hits, Nimble free, Resilient free. Non-Fungible pays when it comes and when it goes. Wealth. Treasure Chest. Golden Bananas. Real money goes onto Logan as Invest Counters, rolls over, deletes a hero at end of turn. Smug Coin. Bamboo Shield." He frowns. "Logan's the smallest hero on the table. Freeze him and the bank stops. Right."
  [ed] "Did he just say freeze my banker? Is that — can they do that? Is it dangerous?"
  [rowan] "Only if someone's watching the gold."
  @deckinfo ed

@scene deck_georgie
  @if deck_known_georgie
    @end
  @choice
    > "That dragon on your bag. Is the deck dragons?" @if georgie_ember @hint Ember is a clue
      [georgie] "…Yes." Barely a whisper. Then, quicker, as if she must say it before she loses the nerve: "Hatchery. Dragons, and eggs. The eggs come first."
      @aff georgie +3 | Noticed Ember
    > "Would it be all right if I asked what you play? You can say no."
      [georgie] "It's — Hatchery. Dragons and eggs. Rubin and Kit and Luna Pele, she's — it's fine. It's a good deck."
      [georgie] "Sorry. I said it too quietly."
      @aff georgie +2 | Asked gently
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_georgie
      @end
  Rowan has gone very still. When he speaks it is to the middle distance, soft and fast.
  [rowan] "…Icy, Flaming, Shimmering eggs. Free, one health. Worthless unless they break on your own turn. Sacrifice them into Green Dragoneer. Every sacrifice-summon, Rubin fires a Destruction spell on top. Black-Thorn Dragon, and neither can be touched by spells. Luna turns burns into cards." A breath. "Tight. Never wastes a trigger."
  [georgie] "You — you know the *order*." She has gone pink to the ears. "Nobody knows the order."
  [rowan] "I saw it online. I've never seen it from this side."
  [georgie] "…It's the best part. Nobody asks about the best part."
  @aff georgie +1 | Knew the order of her deck
  @deckinfo georgie

@scene deck_pippa
  @if deck_known_pippa
    @end
  @choice
    > "I've been wondering what a photographer plays. What's yours?"
      [pippa] "Slimes! They split when you hit them. More of them the worse it gets. Oof, I relate."
      [pippa] "Alice, Stellan the cat, Barker. And a ridiculous amount of Cute Cheese."
      @aff pippa +1 | Asked about her deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_pippa
      @end
  Rowan is looking at the camera, but not through it. His voice comes out of the side of his mouth.
  [rowan] "…Slimy Infestation. Cloudy, Fiery, Shadowy, Splashy, Sparky, Shiny. Every slime does its job the moment it lands. Burn something forever. Freeze. Switch off. Slime Rancher doubles it. Shadowy brings them back. Alice hits for every creature that's sat a turn. Rain of Arrows hits the whole side." A pause. "Wide board that lives a turn is the entire plan."
  [pippa] "Hang on — don't move —" She clicks the shutter. "That. That was your *face*. That was the face of somebody doing arithmetic. Does it do that every time?"
  [rowan] "Every time."
  [pippa] "I'm putting it in the book."
  @aff pippa +2 | Knew her deck
  @deckinfo pippa

@scene deck_mikoto
  @if deck_known_mikoto
    @end
  @choice
    > "Would you mind telling me what you play, Mikoto? I'll understand if you'd rather not."
      [mikoto] "Skeletons. Healers and mages, mostly. Sorry. They heal each other, and when one dies, The Bonegrinder turns it into a card. Is that all right? That's all right."
      @aff mikoto +2 | Asked gently
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_mikoto
      @end
  Rowan's lips are moving. He is not looking at Mikoto any longer. He is looking at a board nobody else can see.
  [rowan] "…Tiny Bone Friends. Healer, Priest, Mage, Wizard. Necromancer brings one back. Treasure Skeleton draws. Bonegrinder turns every dead one into a card. Raise the Minions after a sweep, three at once. Vacarn is the weak point, he's always the weak point." A breath. "Grinds. Doesn't rush. Patient."
  [mikoto] "You — you know all of them? Sorry. Sorry, I — nobody — they only ever know the Death Knight."
  [rowan] "The Death Knight's the dull one. The Healers are the deck."
  [mikoto] "Oh." A small, wet laugh, stopped at once. "Oh, that's — thank you. Sorry. That's lovely."
  @aff mikoto +3 | Knew his deck
  @deckinfo mikoto

@scene deck_gideon
  @if deck_known_gideon
    @end
  @choice
    > "I watched your game with the deckhand. Guardian Beasts, one beside the other, and you never attacked. Guardians of the Treasure Cave?" @if saw_beasts @hint From the game you watched
      [gideon] "Ma, Hou, Hu." A very small, very satisfied pause. "You were watching the discard piles. Nobody watches the discard piles."
      @aff gideon +2 | Read his deck
    > "What is it you run, exactly?"
      [gideon] "A deck." Mild. "I should hate to spoil it for someone who might one day have to beat it." He relents, by a quarter of an inch. "Guardians of the Treasure Cave, Vance. I imagine you will meet them again."
      @aff gideon +0 | Asked him outright
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_gideon
      @end
  [rowan] "…Beasts only come down while your own pile's empty. Every one of them deletes cards when it lands. Yours. Mine. First Circle of Hell wipes an odd pile. Zhu skips a turn, eventually. Never attacks first, because every card he plays is a card he can't afford to lose." A breath. "Lets Ma fill both piles. Right."
  [gideon] "How resourceful."
  [rowan] "It only breaks if something lands in your pile and nothing is there to delete it."
  [gideon] "…" He squares his deck against the felt. Once. Twice. "You may keep that thought. I shall be keeping it as well."
  @deckinfo gideon

@scene deck_inya
  @if deck_known_inya
    @end
  @choice
    > "Bunny hairclip, a bunny charm on the deck box. I'm going to guess bunnies." @hint From her look
      [inya] "It is *not* a pile." Instantly. "Hop and Pop. It's a deck. There's a plan."
      @aff inya +2 | Spotted the bunnies
    > "What do you play, Inya? I won't say a word about bunnies."
      [inya] "Hop and Pop. Bunnies." A narrow look. "You promised."
      @aff inya +1 | Asked about her deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_inya
      @end
  Rowan's eyes have unfocused. His voice runs on under his breath.
  [rowan] "…Bubbles soaks the hits. Cute Bunny, Cheering Rabbit, Town Guard, wide and cheap. Haressassins shoot from the turn after they land. Bunny Bombs ticking in the back, and she picks when it goes. Deepsea Idol and Thicket for cover." A pause. "Fast. Thin. Bubbles falls, everything falls."
  [inya] "…" She looks at him for a long moment. "Who told you about Bubbles."
  [rowan] "Nobody. It's the whole deck."
  [inya] "Rude." Quietly, delighted. "Accurate. But rude."
  @aff inya +1 | Understood the plan
  @deckinfo inya

@scene deck_tomi
  @if deck_known_tomi
    @end
  @choice
    > "A binder on your hip and prices in your head. You count what everyone's holding. Gold? Wealth, Treasure Chests, a big pile?" @hint From his look
      [tomi] "Ha! Right pocket, wrong direction." Delighted. "I don't *pile* it, Wildcard. I take yours."
      [tomi] "Free Port. Thieving on all three heroes, Mimics, Pirates, Dirty Smugglers, and every turn your purse is a little emptier."
      @aff tomi +1 | Nearly had it
    > "Is your deck as much of a business as you are? What do you run?"
      [tomi] "Free Port. Smugglers. I take your gold. Thieving on all three heroes, and then I buy with it."
      @aff tomi +1 | Asked about his deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_tomi
      @end
  Rowan has stopped listening to the patter. Under his breath, quick and flat:
  [rowan] "…Thieving. Mimic. Deepsea Pirate. Dirty Smuggler. Golden Abomination redirects the income. Key buys the artifacts out from under you. Smuggler's Pier, so he spends it on the way past. Thieving Strikes, soft hits." A beat. "Answers that cost gold can't be paid for. Gold Trap?"
  [tomi] "Three. And you're the first person who's ever asked that without wanting to rob me."
  @aff tomi +1 | Understood his plan
  @deckinfo tomi

@scene deck_magnus
  @if deck_known_magnus
    @end
  @choice
    > "You change lists every week or two, if I remember right. What's it this week?"
      [magnus] "Whatever the data says." A glance at the tablet. "One-Two-Punch. Ghuanjun, Bill, Elana. Win rate fifty-nine point four." A very small pause. "You remember that."
      @aff magnus +1 | Remembered how he plays
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_magnus
      @end
  Rowan's eyes go to the stylus in Magnus's hand, and stay there, and his voice comes out low and fast.
  [rowan] "…Ferocious Tiger Kick, Blow of the Venom Snake, Whirlwind Strike. Three attacks a turn, the second and third with a bonus. Stun. Discard. Poison. First turn can't kill. Stranglehold and the Sun Sword next turn. Jump in the River keeps the one attacker alive." A breath. "One hero deep. Every attack announced."
  [magnus] "You have looked at the same lists I have."
  [rowan] "Everyone has. It's the best list on the ladder this week."
  [magnus] "…It is." He does not say anything else for a moment. Then, carefully: "It is a clean list. It is not a deck I *love*."
  @aff magnus +1 | Spoke his language
  @deckinfo magnus

@scene deck_noor
  @if deck_known_noor
    @end
  @choice
    > "Would you tell me what you play, Noor?"
      [noor] "To be precise —" She closes the book on her pencil. "Countdown. The Doom Clock. Twenty counters end the game for whoever places the last one." A pause. "It is entirely transparent. It seems only fair to give notice."
      @aff noor +2 | Asked politely
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_noor
      @end
  Rowan's mouth has started moving a half-second before his voice does.
  [rowan] "…Doom Prophecy fetches the Clock with three counters on it. Only she takes them off. Eagle Warrior, Jaguar Warrior — enter by removing one. Basketskull, a fistful off, turned into damage. Warrior of Teocuilatl spends them as shields. Archers shoot when one lands." A breath. "Twentieth one falls on whoever she's picked. Right. Right."
  [noor] "…You have said that in the correct order."
  [rowan] "Transparent, and nearly impossible to interrupt. It's the most honest threat in the format."
  [noor] "Thank you." A very faint, very dry smile. "I have been trying to say that for two years."
  @aff noor +2 | Knew her deck
  @deckinfo noor

@scene deck_livvie
  @if deck_known_livvie
    @end
  @choice
    > "Quick thing — what's in your box, Livvie?"
      [livvie] "Crystal Gifts." Eyes down, a small sideways look to see if it landed. "Cooldin opens the Well on turn one. I give you a card a turn. It sits revealed in your hand, and it breaks something."
      @aff livvie +1 | Asked about her deck
      @scene mutter_livvie
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_livvie
      @end

@scene mutter_livvie
  @if deck_known_livvie
    @end
  Rowan has stopped looking at her. His voice is flat and very fast.
  [rowan] "…Crystal Well. A gift a turn. Crystals break spell levels, shuffling, hero effects, until you pay to get rid of them. Letter of Misinformations takes the best two cards. Mary draws for every gift. Slow, Magic Amber, Spreading Rumor strip the rest of the hand. Laser Volley asks for what's left." A breath. "No board. Heroes like glass."
  [livvie] "…That's all of it." Her voice has gone quite small. "Nobody has ever said all of it."
  [rowan] "It's a gift economy. With teeth."
  [livvie] "…That's what I call it." A tiny, tired smile. "Don't tell anyone I do."
  @aff livvie +2 | Knew her deck
  @deckinfo livvie

@scene deck_jessica
  @if deck_known_jessica
    @end
  @choice
    > "Three caskets of jewellery. Is the deck the same idea? Everything you own piled onto one hero, Sun Sword, Warhorse?" @hint From her caskets
      [jessica] "How lovely." The most gracious tilt of the head. "That was a considered guess. Dowry."
      [jessica] "I out-spend people, Rowan. Willy takes five cards or a pile of gold, and all of it goes into jewellery for Boris."
      @aff jessica +3 | Read her deck
    > "What do you play, Jessica? I'd love to hear what a person with your taste builds."
      [jessica] "Dowry. It is, I am told, an acquired taste: gold, artifacts, and a great deal of patience."
      @aff jessica +1 | Asked about her deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_jessica
      @end
  Rowan's gaze drifts to the nearest casket, and goes through it.
  [rowan] "…Wealth. Treasure Chest. Mimic. A gold pile nobody else has. Sun Sword, Warhorse, the Vampiric Sword when it comes. All on Boris. Heavy Hit stuns, Quick Attack swings again, heals off the damage. Golden Apple borrows a hero of mine." A pause. "Everything she paid for sits on one hero. Freeze him, stun him — the whole dowry sits."
  [jessica] "You read the hero card." She says it quietly. "Most people read the jewellery."
  @deckinfo jessica

@scene deck_ashton
  @if deck_known_ashton
    @end
  @choice
    > "A rose, and you trim the thorns yourself. A flower with a very sharp edge. Rain of Arrows? A thousand small cuts?" @hint From his rose
      [ashton] "Good heavens, no." Genuinely wounded. "The thorns are for the roses, old thing. They are not a *strategy*."
      [ashton] "Spell Industrialization. Pollution. Naturally."
      @aff ashton +1 | Guessed wrong
    > "What do you play, Ashton? I assume it's flashy."
      [ashton] "Spell Industrialization. Pollution. Naturally."
      @aff ashton +1 | Asked about his deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_ashton
      @end
  Rowan's eyes have gone distant. He speaks without moving his head.
  [rowan] "…Pyroblast, as many targets as he likes. One Pollution Token on his own side for each. Every token shrinks the hand. Victorica lifts one a turn. Piranha is summoned by removing one. Spewer fires when one leaves. Rain of Arrows across my whole side." A breath. "Eraser Beam, once a game. Slow start. Zones clog. Power on credit."
  [ashton] "On *credit!*" He is, for a moment, entirely sincere. "Somebody understands the economics."
  [rowan] "It's a very beautiful way to lose, if you misjudge the tokens."
  @deckinfo ashton

@scene deck_victoria
  @if deck_known_victoria
    @end
  @choice
    > "The ribbons, the lace, the parasol. Is the deck pretty things? Birds and butterflies and healers?" @hint From her look
      [victoria] "Yes." A pause as the thought settles. "How did you know that? I am told people do not usually guess it."
      [victoria] "I chose each one because it is lovely. Pretty Things. The Moonlight Butterfly. The Golden Apple. The Rainbow's Arrow."
      @aff victoria +3 | Understood her deck
    > "Which cards do you play, Victoria? I'd like to hear how you choose."
      [victoria] "The lovely ones." A calm blink. "I am told this is not a strategy. I consider it one."
      @aff victoria +1 | Asked about her deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_victoria
      @end
  Rowan's eyes have unfocused, and for a few seconds the words come out without a face behind them.
  [rowan] "…Moonlight Butterfly. Cute Bird, no Phoenix behind it. Rainbow's Arrow. Angelfeather Arrow, an arrow with no attack. Gems, every colour. Heal. Healing Melody. Golden Apple — borrows a hero of mine. Magic Ruby. No engine. No finisher. Wins if I beat myself."
  He blinks. His eyes come back. He has said all of that out loud.
  [rowan] "I'm — that was out loud. I'm sorry. That was a rude thing to say about somebody's cards."
  [victoria] "It was perfectly accurate." She does not seem offended in the least. "I am told it is not a strategy. I consider it one. I should like it very much if you were *kind* about the Golden Apple."
  @deckinfo victoria

@scene deck_sunny
  @if deck_known_sunny
    @end
  @choice
    > "Towel, goggle tan, wet ponytail. Water, then? Deepsea Idols, sharks, something from the deep end?" @hint From her look
      [sunny] "Ha! Right pool, wrong temperature! It's the cold end. **Ice!**"
      [sunny] "Slip 'n Slide. Everything slides, nothing stays where you put it. Drives the control kids mental."
      @aff sunny +2 | Close enough
    > "What do you play? I'm guessing it's something with a lot of splash."
      [sunny] "Slip 'n Slide! Everything slides. No dramas."
      @aff sunny +1 | Asked about her deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_sunny
      @end
  Rowan's mouth moves before his voice does, low and quick.
  [rowan] "…Pengu, Polar, Snobbit, Snowman. Skates for an extra slide. Spikeblock. Whoolmoth once every hero has a creature. Every Slippery slides into the neighbouring hero each turn, and every slide does something. Ingo gets paid per slide." A beat. "Middle hero falls, outer ones aren't neighbours. Right."
  [sunny] "…Oh, he's *good*." She says it to the gulls. "That's the whole weakness and he said it in one go. Rude."
  [rowan] "It's only a weakness if the other side finds the middle hero."
  [sunny] "That's what I said. Rude *and* clever."
  @deckinfo sunny

@scene deck_marit
  @if deck_known_marit
    @end
  @choice
    > "Flame clips, an ember bow tie, a scarf the colour of coals, and you stepped onto a bollard like it was a stage. Let me guess: Phoenix." @hint From her look
      [marit!] "**OH!** *Oh!* He is **GOOD!** Ladies and gentlemen, the stranger has **SEEN** me!"
      [marit!] "**PHOENIX ENCORE!** The *rise!* The *fall!* The **RISE AGAIN!**"
      @aff marit +3 | Read her from her look
    > "What do you play, Marit?"
      [marit!] "**Phoenix Encore!** A *grand* revival, a discard pile in a *petting zoo!* Cute Cat, Cute Dog, Cute **PHOENIX!**"
      @aff marit +2 | Asked about her deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_marit
      @end
  Rowan has put one hand over his mouth. Behind it his voice is a steady, level murmur.
  [rowan] "…Cute Bird in front. It dies, she discards two, a Phoenix comes off the deck. Cats mill three. Dog comes back out of the pile. Skull Necklace pays on the way down. Glass of Marbles. Gravedigger Slap for every differently named creature in the pile." A breath. "Right. *Right.*"
  [marit] "Is he — is he doing a *monologue?* He's doing a **monologue!** Ladies and gentlemen —"
  [rowan] "Sorry. Sorry. The pile's the engine, not the graveyard. That's all."
  [marit!] "It is the **SECOND ACT!** *Thank* you!"
  @deckinfo marit

@scene deck_rana
  @if deck_known_rana
    @end
  @if rana_pressed
    @end
  @choice
    > "Do you play? I'm not asking for a game. I just don't know what anybody's running."
      @scene answer_rana
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_rana
      @end

@scene answer_rana
  @if deck_known_rana
    @end
  [rana] "…" A very long pause. The scowl does not change. Something in her shoulders does. "Debug Mode."
  [rana] "Face-down cards. They each wait for one thing you do." A shrug that tries very hard to be indifferent. "It's not interesting."
  @aff rana +1 | Asked, and didn't push
  Rowan says nothing for a moment. Then, so low she may not be meant to hear:
  [rowan] "…Cybug LOCUST copies whatever you attach to my hero. LADYBUG cancels an Ability. ANTS punishes damage that doesn't kill. Bee, Centipede, Rhinoceros, Scarab. Each one waits for exactly one thing. Bakhm hits for every trap that fires. Paid for by deleting the matching artifact." A breath. "Troop Annihilation refills them. Nobody plays it like that."
  [rana] "…You read the names." Under her breath. "Nobody reads the names."
  [rana] "Whatever."
  @flag rana_deck_talk
  @deckinfo rana

@scene deck_teobalt
  @if deck_known_teobalt
    @end
  @choice
    > "A clipboard, a rota, a list for everything. You'd play something that makes rules. Control? A lock?" @hint From his clipboard
      [teobalt] "Three things." Brightly. "One: yes. Two: *yes*. Three: I can't believe you guessed it."
      [teobalt] "Order of Tusca. Hatusbal forbids shuffling, and every Tuscan adds another clause."
      @aff teobalt +2 | Read his deck
    > "What do you play, Teobalt? I'd guess it involves procedure."
      [teobalt] "Order of Tusca. Control. Hatusbal makes it impossible to shuffle, and each creature adds a clause." A very small, very pleased pause. "Yes, that is how it sounds."
      @aff teobalt +1 | Asked about his deck
    > Let the cards wait for now.
      @flag deck_skipped_teobalt
      @end
  Rowan has taken a half-step back. His voice is low and exact, as if reading from a sheet.
  [rowan] "…Aristocrat, Artist, Mystic, Prisoner. Each one a clause. No Potions. No multi-card draws. No extra gold. Natas makes a Master's Plan every turn and cancels the one card that mattered. Slow. Icy Grave. Forbidden Zone. Mr. Jiggles and a Haressassin grind for the damage." A breath. "Plain mid-sized bodies. One Master's Plan a turn, no more."
  [teobalt] "…You are describing my deck." A very quiet, very serious voice. "That is the most accurate description I have ever heard of my deck, including my own."
  @aff teobalt +1 | Knew his deck
  @deckinfo teobalt

# ───────────────────────────── NACHGESPRÄCHE ─────────────────────────────
#  Ein Duell zeigt das Deck: auch ohne vorheriges Gespräch gilt es danach als bekannt.

@scene post_baylee
  @if not deck_known_baylee
    @deckinfo baylee
  @if won:ferry_baylee
    Baylee turns his hand over, one big dinosaur at a time, and studies the board.
    [baylee] "You didn't attack at all."
    [rowan] "I waited until you'd stacked your Summoning Magic and then I killed the hero that would have called the Chimera. You never got to call it."
    [baylee] "Huh." Slowly. "Good animal, that one. Big. Never got out of the barn."
    [rowan] "If I'd let the Chimera land I'd have lost. It's the best card in your deck."
    [baylee] "Don't tell Nathan I said that. He'd put it on a T-shirt."
  @else
    Baylee sets down his last giant. It is, you notice, almost apologetic.
    [baylee] "Sorry. Chimera came down on turn six."
    [rowan] "I should have killed Alex when he was still doing nothing. Everything else was built around him."
    [baylee] "That's right." Pleased, and visibly embarrassed about being pleased. "You'd have to get him early. Most folks don't."
    [baylee] "Your storm's something, though. Hit three of my big ones at once. I'd not seen that."
  @aff baylee +1 | Talked it through

@scene post_ed
  @if not deck_known_ed
    @deckinfo ed
  @if won:ferry_ed
    Ed is flat on his back on the planks with his hat on his chest, grinning at the sky.
    [ed] "Whoa. I didn't see the Storm come back around. It just — kept zapping! Every turn! Is that allowed?"
    [rowan] "That's the whole deck. Gathering Storm attaches to a hero and keeps hitting three of your targets at the start of every turn."
    [ed] "Three! Every turn! My bananas didn't stand a chance." He sits up. "I gained a lot of gold, though. Did you see how much gold I gained?"
    [rowan] "I saw. If I hadn't destroyed Logan, that bank would have woken every Monkee at once."
  @else
    Ed leaps up and does a lap of the rail, hat held on with one hand.
    [ed] "I WON! Did you see Logan? Did you see how much gold? It was like a bank robbery but the other way!"
    [rowan] "You gained gold on three different turns and a Monkee woke up every time. I couldn't keep up."
    [ed] "That's the whole deck!" He grins. "It's a good deck, right? It wasn't just the hat."
    [rowan] "It wasn't the hat. Although the hat helps."
  @aff ed +1 | Talked it through

@scene post_georgie
  @if not deck_known_georgie
    @deckinfo georgie
  @if won:ferry_georgie
    Georgie is looking at her last egg, which is still unbroken. She has gone very quiet.
    [georgie] "I couldn't break it. They only pay when they break on my turn, and you never let me have a turn where it mattered."
    [rowan] "I killed Rubin before she could sacrifice. If she'd survived one more turn the eggs would have broken in your favour."
    [georgie] "You noticed Rubin." A very small voice. "Usually they notice the dragons."
    [rowan] "The dragons are just what she throws."
    A tiny, astonished smile.
    [georgie] "That's — yes. That's what Pippa says."
  @else
    Georgie has already stacked her cards into a tidy pile and is holding Ember, the green plush dragon, on her knee.
    [georgie] "Sorry."
    [rowan] "You don't have to say sorry."
    [georgie] "I always do. I can't stop." A pause. "You attacked on turn four. I thought you'd attack on turn three."
    [rowan] "I wanted to see whether you'd break an egg early. You didn't, and then it was too late for me."
    [georgie] "Everyone breaks an egg early." She looks at her hands. "You're the first person who waited."
  @aff georgie +1 | Talked it through

@scene post_mikoto
  @if not deck_known_mikoto
    @deckinfo mikoto
  @if won:ferry_mikoto
    Mikoto is looking at the board with wide, unfocused eyes. A skeleton at the bottom of his discard pile has not quite finished falling over.
    [mikoto] "Sorry — oh. Sorry. You killed all my healers before they could heal anything. I didn't — that's — that's good. That's what you should do."
    [rowan] "I went after the Necromancer first. If he'd survived, Raise the Minions would have brought three back."
    [mikoto] "It would have! It would have, wouldn't it? I had it in my hand!" A giggle, then quick embarrassment. "Sorry. It was a very good plan."
  @else
    Mikoto stares at his board, and then at you, and then bursts into a breathless laugh that is half relief.
    [mikoto] "I won! I'm sorry, I'm so — I won. The Bonegrinder came down on turn five and it turned every skeleton you killed into a card."
    [rowan] "I should have left them alone. Every time I killed one I was drawing for you."
    [mikoto] "Nothing's ever properly finished." Quietly, for him. "That's — I've been trying to say that for years."
  @aff mikoto +1 | Talked it through

@scene post_ashton
  @if not deck_known_ashton
    @deckinfo ashton
  @if won:ferry_ashton
    Ashton regards a board that is mostly smoke.
    [ashton] "I over-leaked. I always over-leak. It's a vice."
    [rowan] "You Pyroblasted three targets on turn two and your hand shrank to four cards. Then I could just wait."
    [ashton] "A sound plan. Waiting for me to run out of hand." He smiles ruefully. "It's the one thing I can't afford, old thing. A patient opponent."
    [rowan] "Then I'll be patient."
  @else
    Ashton sweeps the last cards together with a flourish.
    [ashton] "I do hope the lady was watching."
    [rowan] "You Pyroblasted everything I put down and then laundered the tokens through the Piranhas. I didn't have an answer."
    [ashton] "Do tell her that." He glances at Jessica, who is looking at the sea. "…Or don't. I'll tell her myself."
  @aff ashton +1 | Talked it through

@scene post_sunny
  @if not deck_known_sunny
    @deckinfo sunny
  @if won:ferry_sunny
    Sunny is still on her face on the planks, counting push-ups aloud, and then rolls over with a grin and a towel on her face.
    [sunny] "Ten! No dramas! Nobody told me you'd go for the Whoolmoth first."
    [rowan] "It was the only card that could slide into three of my heroes. If it landed, I'd have lost."
    [sunny] "It never landed. Clever." She sits up. "I like your storm. It doesn't slide. It just waits."
  @else
    You are lying next to a seagull on your back, arms burning. Sunny rolls onto her side, propping her head on one hand.
    [sunny] "That was a proper game! Everything slides, and you kept the Spikeblock off your Hero for four turns. That's hard."
    [rowan] "I couldn't stop the Snowman, though. That froze me in position for a turn and I couldn't use the spell."
    [sunny] "That's the trick." Cheerfully. "You can't stop everything. You can only choose what hurts less."
  @aff sunny +1 | Talked it through

@scene post_marit
  @if not deck_known_marit
    @deckinfo marit
  @if won:ferry_marit
    [marit!] "**ALAS!** *DEFEAT!* And what a defeat, ladies and gentlemen — the **GREATEST** defeat of the **MORNING!**"
    The crowd, which has grown to a dozen, applauds. Marit takes a very small, very private bow and drops, mid-flourish, into her ordinary voice.
    [marit] "That was the Storm. It never stopped hitting. I couldn't get a Phoenix to stay on the board for more than a turn."
    [rowan] "The Cute Bird died while you only had one card in hand. You couldn't discard two, so nothing came off the deck. After that I just kept the Phoenix off the table."
    [marit] "You *starved* the Bird. Oh, that's cold." A bright, delighted laugh. "I love it. Nobody's ever had the nerve."
    [rowan] "Your deck is gorgeous. I mean it. The discard pile as an engine. I'd never have built it."
    [marit] "*Thank* you. I stay up at night thinking nobody understands it." She looks, for a second, entirely sincere. "You do."
  @else
    [marit!] "**THE PHOENIX!** Ladies and gentlemen, **BEHOLD** — the *PHOENIX!* **ALWAYS** the Phoenix!"
    She takes a bow so deep her scarf trails on the planks. The small crowd cheers. And then she drops, mid-flourish, into her ordinary voice, the quick, wry one.
    [marit] "That was lovely. Thank you for letting me. Your Storm was very hard to play around."
    [rowan] "I held Chain Lightning for three turns and you discarded two Cute Cats. I thought I had you, and then the Cute Bird died and the Phoenix came back."
    [marit] "From the ashes of my frankly terrible opening hand." A beat. "I had no idea that would work. I really didn't."
    [rowan] "It works because you're willing to throw cards away. Most people can't."
    [marit!] "It's the **ONLY** thing I'm good at!"
  [marit] "Properly, by the way, it's Marit. Not the bow tie one. Come and find me at the commentary desk, Rowan Vance. I'll tell you *everything*."
  @aff marit +1 | Talked it through

@scene post_noor
  @if not deck_known_noor
    @deckinfo noor
  @if won:ferry_noor
    [noor] "To be precise, you did not win on time. You won on the board." She turns her last card face up. "I had four counters on the Clock and no way to use them."
    [rowan] "I killed your Warriors before they could remove counters. If one had landed I'd have been two turns from losing."
    [noor] "It was a very clean read." Quiet, honest. "I have not been beaten by a read in a long time."
  @else
    [noor] "I announced it on turn two." A faint, almost mischievous pause. "The Doom Clock reached twenty on turn nine. You were still surprised."
    [rowan] "I was. I knew it was coming and I still couldn't stop it. Every counter I tried to remove, you took back."
    [noor] "That is the value of notice. It does not help the person who receives it."
    [rowan] "That's the best advertisement for a deck I've ever heard."
  @aff noor +1 | Talked it through

@scene post_livvie
  @if not deck_known_livvie
    @deckinfo livvie
  @if won:ferry_livvie
    Livvie counts the five credits twice, each coin with great precision.
    [livvie] "Quick thing — your Gathering Storm broke a Crystal I handed you. Did you notice?"
    [rowan] "I noticed. I played around the Well by not taking the first one. It cost me tempo."
    [livvie] "That's the intended counter." She looks, unexpectedly, impressed. "Nobody works it out. They all take the gift."
  @else
    Livvie takes your five credits, then, a half-second later, hands three of them back without looking at you.
    [livvie] "The Crystal Well gave you a Crystal on turn one and you used it to break my own spell level."
    [rowan] "That was the whole deck: turn her own present against her."
    [livvie] "Nobody does that." Eyes down, a small sideways look. "It was quite clever. Don't say I said so."
  @aff livvie +1 | Talked it through

@scene post_magnus
  @if not deck_known_magnus
    @deckinfo magnus
  @if won:ferry_magnus
    Magnus is staring at the tablet. He has already started a note.
    [magnus] "One-Two-Punch cannot kill on the first turn. You knew that. You used the first turn to set up a Storm that kills before the second."
    [rowan] "It kills on the third. I wasn't racing you. I was making you commit."
    [magnus] "Commit." A thin, careful smile that looks almost real. "I committed. And you did not."
    [rowan] "I don't think the deck you run is the point. The point is what you do when the list stops working."
    [magnus] "That is not a comfortable sentence."
  @else
    Magnus makes a clean note on the tablet. Forty-one and one.
    [magnus] "Casual, ferry, unofficial. It did not count." But there is a look in his face that is not quite a smile. "Your Storm was well timed."
    [rowan] "You hit me three times a turn. I had one turn to answer."
    [magnus] "And yet you did not hurry." He looks up. "I would very much like to understand how you do that."
    [rowan] "Honestly? I don't know."
  @aff magnus +1 | Talked it through

@scene post_inya
  @if not deck_known_inya
    @deckinfo inya
  @if won:ferry_inya
    Inya looks at the board for a long time. Her last bunny is still on it.
    [inya] "I should have set off the Bomb on turn five."
    [rowan] "You waited because you wanted to see whether I'd kill Bubbles. I didn't, and that was the mistake."
    [inya] "Don't be nice." Quick, sharp, almost cheerful. "You attacked the Haressassins instead of the hero. They're my whole clock."
    [rowan] "They were the only part of it I could actually reach."
  @else
    Inya's bunnies are scattered across the table in an enormous, happy mess.
    [inya] "That was *my* turn five. You kept the Bomb ticking and you didn't set it off, and it took three of your heroes down with it."
    [rowan] "I tried to wait you out. You didn't blink."
    [inya] "Rabbits turn ninety degrees at full speed." Pointed, and very pleased with herself. "Name one of your storm clouds that can do that."
  @aff inya +1 | Talked it through
